; VIRTBLK.EXE's description, for cargo drivers: it goes into the zip as
; VIRTBLK.INF (with Source= added) and into the boot catalog the kernel
; carries as one line per [Devices] entry. Raise Version= for every change
; that is published.
; The devices of the kernel's built-in virtio-blk driver, which this driver
; replaces (D-280): the transitional device (1001) and the modern-only one
; (1042), both driven through the modern (virtio 1.x) interface.
; Boot=Yes: a boot driver (D-254), carried inside FREEHOLD's kernel file and
; started before C: is mounted, so it is left out of the online catalog: it
; is updated with the kernel.
[Driver]
Name=VIRTBLK
Version=1.0.0-1
File=VIRTBLK.EXE
Description=virtio block device (virtio 1.x)
Licence=MIT
Basic=Yes
Boot=Yes

[Devices]
1AF4:1001 storage
1AF4:1042 storage
